// Combinatorial gene regulation — expression as localisation + logic.
//
// A transcription factor does nothing until it is physically inside the
// nucleus. Import is gated by the nuclear pore; here two compartments are
// two rooms and the pore is a door(to). A signal frees an activator (its
// inhibitor is degraded) and it translocates through the pore; a second
// signal imports a coactivator; a repressor is exported. The gene fires
// only when BOTH activators are in the nucleus AND the repressor is gone —
// a coincidence detector, the reason gene control needs logic and not just
// presence.
//
// The division of labour is the whole point. WHERE each factor is, over
// time, is what the 3D emits — whereabouts, in/4, derived from the proteins
// actually moving through the pore. WHETHER the gene is on is what Prolog
// derives from those facts (rules.pl):
//     expressed(Acts, Reps, R, T) :- all_present(Acts,R,T), none_present(Reps,R,T).
// Code and Prolog are cool, but they don't know 3D — so the 3D is the
// compiler that pushes back: you cannot claim a gene is expressed unless the
// factors really reached the nucleus through the pore. Forget to import one
// and expressed/4 fails — awaiting/4 names the signal you still owe.
//
// (Diagram convention: the nucleus sits beside the cytoplasm rather than
// within it. What the model needs is the topology — two compartments, one
// gated pore — not the enclosure.)

theme blueprint
view top

time basal 2     // before any signal: only the repressor is in the nucleus
time early 10    // one signal in — the gene must still wait for the second
time active 15   // both activators imported, repressor exported: ON

// two compartments, one gated connection — the pore is a door(to)
room cytoplasm size(9 2.5 7) door(to nucleus 1.0)
room nucleus size(5 2.5 7) right-of(cytoplasm)

// the gene, a locus in the nucleus — grey until it fires
box gene size(0.5 0.5 0.5) at(nucleus 1.2 0) color(#8892a0)

// activator A, held in the cytoplasm by an inhibitor bound to it
cylinder tf_a r(0.25) h(1.0) at(cytoplasm -2.5 -1.5) color(#c8451f)
box inhibitor size(0.5 0.5 0.5) at(cytoplasm -2.5 -0.6) vanish(4) color(#3a4150)

// activator B (a coactivator), cytoplasmic, awaiting a second signal
cylinder tf_b r(0.25) h(1.0) at(cytoplasm -2.5 1.5) color(#b98a1d)

// the repressor, on the gene in the nucleus, holding it off
cylinder repressor r(0.25) h(1.0) at(nucleus 1.0 0) color(#1f7a6d)

set activators tf_a tf_b
set repressors repressor

// --- signal 1 (t=4): inhibitor degraded; A imported; repressor exported ---
walk tf_a to(cytoplasm-nucleus-door) start(4) over(2)
walk tf_a to(nucleus 1.2 -1.5) over(2)
walk repressor to(cytoplasm-nucleus-door) start(4) over(2)
walk repressor to(cytoplasm 2 0) over(2)

// --- signal 2 (t=9): coactivator B imported through the pore --------------
walk tf_b to(cytoplasm-nucleus-door) start(9) over(2)
walk tf_b to(nucleus 1.2 1.5) over(2)

// transcription switches on once the last condition is met
paint gene to(#e8b923) start(13) over(2)

// --- the localisation, in language ---------------------------------------
check adjacent(cytoplasm nucleus)               // the pore really connects them
? when in(tf_a nucleus)                          // imported at signal 1...
? when in(tf_b nucleus)                          // ...B not until signal 2
? when in(repressor nucleus)                     // present until exported
check never in(tf_a nucleus) during(0 4)         // A is held out until its signal
check in(tf_a nucleus) at(active)
check in(tf_b nucleus) at(active)

// --- the regulation, derived ---------------------------------------------
?- expressed(activators, repressors, nucleus, basal)   // off — no activators in
?- awaiting(activators, nucleus, early, X)             // X = tf_b: one signal short
?- expressed(activators, repressors, nucleus, early)   // still off — AND gate unmet
?- expressed(activators, repressors, nucleus, active)  // ON — both in, repressor gone
